  'insight.label': 'Resources',
  'insight.title': 'Building AI-ready data foundations in healthcare',
  'insight.byline': 'By the Health Cloud Product team',
  'insight.excerpt': 'How a structured, interoperable, secure-by-default patient record becomes the real precondition for clinical AI and automation at your institution.',
  'insight.cta': 'Read the article',
  'insight.body': "Many healthcare institutions approach artificial intelligence tool-first: a chatbot, a triage assistant, an imaging model. But even the most impressive AI is worthless if it sits on patient data scattered across spreadsheets, paper files, and systems that don't talk to each other.\n\nThe real foundation is a single, structured, timestamped, interoperable patient record: every visit, prescription, and lab result tied to the same patient identifier, in a consistent schema, available in real time to authorized staff and to third-party systems through a documented API.\n\nThat is exactly the bet behind Health Cloud: a clean, normalized clinical data core (patients, consultations, prescriptions, lab, radiology, billing) exposed both through a human interface built for care teams, and through a REST API for your future automation or AI projects.\n\nIn practice, that means medical records that never get lost between departments, reliable statistics without manual re-entry, and a sound base for the day your institution wants to plug in a clinical decision-support tool.\n\nStart small: centralize patients, appointments, and prescriptions first. Everything else — advanced reporting, third-party integrations, future AI modules — builds naturally once the data itself is clean.",
